+# Agent Note: Responses multi-tool reasoning replay
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-18-responses-multi-tool-reasoning-replay.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Some DeepSeek-compatible Responses gateways require every historical `function_call` to be immediately followed by its matching `function_call_output`. pi-ai normally flattens one assistant response as all reasoning, commentary, and calls, then appends all following tool results. A multi-call turn therefore becomes `call1, call2, output1, output2`, and the gateway reports `No tool output found for tool call call1` even though that output is present later.
+
+## Decision
+
+The pi-ai provider profile exposes `repeatReasoningBeforeEachToolCallModels` as an opt-in model list restricted to `openai-responses`. Before dispatch for a named model, the adapter projects a completed multi-call turn as `signed prelude, call1, output1, signed prelude, call2, output2`. The prelude contains the complete native `thinkingSignature`, including encrypted content, plus commentary emitted before the first call. The durable session message remains unchanged.
+
+Unsigned reasoning cannot reconstruct a native Responses item and is not repeated. Projection occurs only when every call in the run has a matching result, so incomplete histories are left intact. Single-call turns and every route using another protocol retain their existing request history.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Change every Responses request.** Standard OpenAI-compatible endpoints do not require the duplicate item, so unconditional projection could introduce invalid repeated item identifiers or change cache behavior.
+
+**Patch the installed pi-ai package.** A package-manager patch does not propagate to consumers of the published Harness packages, and editing `node_modules` disappears on reinstall.
+
+**Disable parallel tool calls.** DeepSeek-compatible gateways may ignore that request option, and serial model behavior does not repair existing multi-call history.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Deployments must list only models served by a gateway with this validation rule. The session log remains the source of the original response; the configured route deterministically projects adjacent call/output pairs. Unit coverage pins commentary preludes, unsigned reasoning, result matching, multi-call ordering, unknown-model and protocol validation, and adapter-dispatch behavior.
